  "body": "Read the ongoing API method tracker into `apiMethodTracker` in the steps to abort a `NavigateEvent`. The existing step checks that tracker for null and then passes an unbound `apiMethodTracker` to the promise rejection algorithm. The new binding supplies the checked tracker at the same point in the steps.\n\nThe existing [stop test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/e3baabe076221e80d9c07d9aea2cbefa7ad656b6/navigation-api/ordering-and-transition/navigate-intercept-stop.html) and [interception rejection test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/e3baabe076221e80d9c07d9aea2cbefa7ad656b6/navigation-api/ordering-and-transition/navigate-same-document-intercept-reject.html) both assert that the navigation result’s `finished` promise rejects after the `committed` promise has been fulfilled.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13247/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 10:55 AM UTC (591de8a)\">/nav-history-apis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13247/91052e8...591de8a/nav-history-apis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 10:55 AM UTC (591de8a)\">diff</a> )",
